        "original_id": "98ba5329-8ef2-5063-b9c1-75faaf289526",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Chamaelirium, Chamaelirium luteum, Hovea\n- Topics: plant taxonomy, common names, native range\n\nFacts:\n- Chamaelirium is a genus of flowering plants that contains the single species Chamaelirium luteum.\n- Chamaelirium luteum is commonly known as blazing-star, devil's bit, false unicorn, fairy wand, and helonias.\n- Hovea, also called purple pea, is a genus of perennial shrubs.\n- Hovea is native to Australia.",
